  previous: { A: null, B: "A"}
}
```
- The function reconstructPath in Dijkstra takes in previous (an object), start , and goal and returns an array representing the shortest path from start to goal.
- The function minimumSpanningTree in Kruskal takes in the graph (a Graph instance) and returns an object containing mstEdges (an array of edges in the MST) and totalWeight (the sum of the edge weights in the MST).
